    2. Tile it across a 27x27 grid to get the output
    3. Place 4-5 non-overlapping rectangular holes (2-6 rows x 2-6 cols each) at random positions with Chebyshev gap >= 2; optionally merge two adjacent rectangles into an L-shape
    4. Verify all 64 tile phases remain visible after masking; if not, shrink or shift a hole and retry
    5. Set hole cells to black (0) to produce the input
